    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "title": "Recognise, don't memorise",
      "text": "You don't need to type commands yourself. This series teaches you to *recognise* a handful and the ideas behind them. On a Mac the terminal speaks **zsh**; bash works the same for almost everything here (the one difference, a pattern that matches no files, is in A5, *Patterns*).",
